From d5bd67c1b76ce590525751ca646bc187ef43096e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:18:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] XHTTP: Let a flow governor stream hold a frame whatever
 the stack is shown, drop the queue

The queue of streams the send window kept credit from missed room the server
freed, walked itself for every client frame where the room was under a
quantum, and gave freed room to the oldest stream instead of the one whose
reader reads.

What it was for is one case: after a client's lowering of its window the
stack can be shown less than a client returns credit for, and a stream
opened then at a full limit sent nothing that would bring credit of its own.
A stream may now hold a frame whatever the stack is shown, by credit where
the stack was shown less, and needs nobody to wake it. The queue is gone.
